.Dd September 17, 2026
.Dt GOLDOUT 1
.Os "macOS"
.Sh NAME
.Nm /usr/local/bin/goldout
.Nd Join AppleDouble files into two-fork HFS resource files.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h , Fl \-help
.Op Fl q , Fl \-quiet
.Op Fl \-nosetinfo
.Op Fl \-nodelete
.Op Fl \-version
.Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Goldout is the counterpart to 
.Xr SplitForks 1 
or 
.Xr goldin 1 .
Goldin will recursively traverse any directory passed to it looking for
AppleDouble files. So long as the directories are on an HFS or HFS+ volume
and there is a matching main (data fork) file goldout will unite each pair
as one two-forked file whose resource fork can be accessed by Resource 
Manager calls or via the ..namedfork/rsrc path method.
.Pp
Goldin exists because in later versions of Max OS X (Sierra onwards) the
Apple provided /System/Library/CoreServices/FixupResourceForks is missing.
.Pp
.Nm
accepts these flags and arguments:
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print usage information.
.It Fl q , Fl \-quiet
No diagnostic output.
.It Fl \-nosetinfo
Don't set type, creator, flags, permissions.
.It Fl \-nodelete
Don't delete the AppleDouble file after adding the resource fork and metadata
to the main file.
.It Fl \-version
Display the tool's version.
.It Ar path ...
One or more directories to examine. Goldout willl not accept files passed as arguments.
.El
.Pp
.Sh FILES
.Bl  -tag -width -indent
.It example
Data fork file
.It \._example
AppleDouble encoded resource fork and metadata.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Goldout will do nothing if the directory is on an APFS volime.
.Pp
Goldout lives here: https://github.com/packagesdev/goldout.
.Sh SEE ALSO 
.Xr SplitForks 1 , 
.Xr FixupResourceForks 1 , 
.Xr goldin 1 , 
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 1740 documents AppleSingle/AppleDouble formats.